{
  "id": "champions-league",
  "name": "Champions League",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Champions League is the Pokémon Card Game's series of large official tournaments in Japan, held in major cities every season since 2017, with junior, senior and master leagues and entry by application, drawn by lottery when too many apply. Its first season was seven tournaments from February to June 2017, which earned Championship Points toward Japan's national final. From the 2018 season each season has run from September to August, normally with four or five tournaments, though COVID-19 canceled several from the spring of 2020 to the autumn of 2021. In the 2021 season, and again from the 2023 season, the tournaments gave no Championship Points; their top finishers were invited to the World Championships instead, from 2023 the top four of each league.\n\nThe top finishers of each league win the series' trophy card, never sold or given to entrants, in a print for their place (the 3rd Place print goes to both the third and the fourth) with the year and city on it: Victory Decoration from 2017, Victory Proof from Champions League 2020 Aichi in December 2019, and Victory Symbol from Champions League 2023 Aichi in February 2023, reprinted for the Mega Evolution era in 2026. The name echoes the Champion's League, Japan's invitation-only national final from 2000 to 2007.",
